-
-# OpenShift CLI Shim
-
-Use this skill when working with `shims/oc`, `shims/oc_4_18`,
-`shims/oc_4_20`, `shims/oc_4_22`, their tests, docs, installer wiring, or
-OpenShift CLI usage through Shimmy.
-
-## Files
-
-- Dispatcher shim: `../../../shims/oc`
-- Minor shims: `../../../shims/oc_4_18`, `../../../shims/oc_4_20`,
-  `../../../shims/oc_4_22`
-- Shim configs: `../../../shims/oc_4_18.conf`,
-  `../../../shims/oc_4_20.conf`, `../../../shims/oc_4_22.conf`
-- User docs: `../../../docs/shims/oc.md`
-- Tests: `../../../scripts/test-shimmy.sh`
-- Installer/status/update wiring: `../../../lib/repo/shimmy-catalog.sh`,
-  `../../../scripts/status-shimmy.sh`, `../../../scripts/update-shimmy.sh`
-- README: `../../../README.md`
-- Contributor guidance: `../../../CONTRIBUTING.md`
-- Shared prompt: `../../../docs/prompt-shimmy-project.md`
-
-## Installed Workflow
-
-When this skill is installed outside the Shimmy source checkout, prefer activated
-commands such as `SHIMMY_OC_VERSION=4.20 oc version`, inspect selected profile
-state with `shimmy status --format manifest`, and use
-`SHIMMY_PROFILE_ACTIVE=upstream SHIMMY_OC_VERSION=4.20 oc version` when
-validating the upstream profile. Use repo-local paths such as `./shims/oc_4_20`
-only when intentionally editing or testing source files in the Shimmy checkout.
-
-## Current Behavior
-
-- User command: `oc`, which dispatches based on `SHIMMY_OC_VERSION`
-- Supported versions: `4.18`, `4.20`, `4.22`
-- Minor shim images:
-  - `SHIMMY_OC_4_18_IMAGE`, default
-    `docker-redhat-proxy.northgrum.com/openshift4/ose-cli:4.18`
-  - `SHIMMY_OC_4_20_IMAGE`, default
-    `docker-redhat-proxy.northgrum.com/openshift4/ose-cli:4.20`
-  - `SHIMMY_OC_4_22_IMAGE`, default
-    `docker-redhat-proxy.northgrum.com/openshift4/ose-cli:4.22`
-- Pull overrides: `SHIMMY_OC_4_18_IMAGE_PULL=always`,
-  `SHIMMY_OC_4_20_IMAGE_PULL=always`, `SHIMMY_OC_4_22_IMAGE_PULL=always`
-- Runtime mode: `-i` by default, `-it` when stdin and stdout are terminals
-- Mounts:
-  - `$PWD` to `/work`
-  - `$HOME/.kube` to `/root/.kube:ro` when present
-  - `$HOME/.config/oc` to `/root/.config/oc:ro` when present
-- Entrypoint: forced to `oc`
-- Platform: shared Podman helper resolves `linux/amd64` on Linux and
-  `linux/arm64` on macOS
-
-## Change Rules
-
-1. Keep `SHIMMY_OC_VERSION` version-agnostic; do not encode the major version in
-   the selector env var name.
-2. Add new minor tracks as `oc_<major>_<minor>` shims with matching `.conf`
-   files and catalog/status/update/docs entries.
-3. Preserve read-only kube/oc config mounts unless a task explicitly changes
-   credential behavior.
-4. Keep the dispatcher Podman-free; container invocation belongs in the minor
-   shims.
-5. Update runtime shims, configs, catalog/status/update wiring, docs, README,
-   and tests together when behavior changes.
-
-## Validation
-
-- Dispatcher missing selector: `./shims/oc --preview-shim version`
-- Dispatcher preview: `SHIMMY_OC_VERSION=4.20 ./shims/oc --preview-shim version`
-- Direct minor preview: `./shims/oc_4_20 --preview-shim version`
-- Live smoke, when the registry is reachable: `./shims/oc_4_20 version`
-- Installed smoke: `shimmy test --shim oc_4_20`
-
-## Learning Guidance
-
-- The dispatcher maps any syntactically valid `major.minor` selector to
-  `oc_<major>_<minor>` and then requires that executable to exist. This keeps
-  future `5.x` support limited to adding the minor shim and its metadata.
-- Use preview checks before live smoke because the configured image may live in
-  a private registry and require host credentials or network access.
